From 6a9854c9f3f62ebe3d7ba6a6dab6d9feae63cc78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:25:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 111/116] MAS local: put out the maximize button's highlight
 after a click

The lean window's maximize / restore button is HTMAXBUTTON to Windows, so
the window works out its highlight from the non-client mouse messages and
asks for WM_NCMOUSELEAVE (TrackMouseEvent, TME_LEAVE | TME_NONCLIENT) to
put it out. It asked only on WM_NCMOUSEMOVE. A WM_NCLBUTTONDOWN,
WM_NCLBUTTONDBLCLK or WM_NCLBUTTONUP over the button with no move before
it lights the button too, and then no leave message came: the highlight
stayed after the mouse had gone onto the guest screen or another window.

The window now asks for the leave message after any of these messages
that leaves the button lit (needsLeaveNotice() in lean-window-frame). The
snap layouts of Windows 11 over the button are unchanged: WM_NCHITTEST
still answers HTMAXBUTTON there.

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#214

Change-Id: Ie5bddd28a3b40c111d24ffdac92ffd5f0febdcfb
